---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../../styles/stats.css";

const REPO = "https://github.com/straf10/EuroHoops-Analytics";
const AUTHOR = "https://github.com/straf10";
const root = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const description =
  "6.75 Analytics is a free EuroLeague stats and forecast site made by one person. What it is for, how to read it, and how it stays independent.";
---

<Base title="About" description={description} current="about">
  <header class="wrap head">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      6.75 Analytics is a free home for EuroLeague numbers: player and team stats, and forecasts that are kept on
      record. The name is the distance of the three-point line in metres.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap about">
    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="why-title">
      <h2 id="why-title">Why it exists</h2>
      <p>
        EuroLeague box scores are easy to find one game at a time and hard to find in any other shape. This site puts
        the numbers in a form you can sort, compare and follow across seasons.
      </p>
      <p>
        It also holds itself to its forecasts. Before every 2026-27 EuroLeague game, a forecast is logged in public.
        Once tip-off passes it is never edited, and after the game it is scored against the result. The record is
        there for anyone to check.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="who-title">
      <h2 id="who-title">Who builds it</h2>
      <p>
        One person builds and runs it. The questions, the code and the mistakes are all theirs. To reach them, or to
        report an error, use
        <a class="ink-link" href={AUTHOR}>GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="read-title">
      <h2 id="read-title">How to read it</h2>
      <p>
        The stats come from the EuroLeague's public API, which is unofficial. Every response is saved, and the site
        shows the latest five EuroLeague seasons. It refreshes once a day, and the footer shows the date of the last
        build.
      </p>
      <p>
        Early in a season a few games decide every average, so read small samples with care. Forecasts are chances,
        not promises: a side given 70% should lose about three times in ten.
      </p>
      <p>
        Unsure what a column means? The <a class="ink-link" href={`${root}/glossary/`}>glossary</a> explains each term
        the site shows, and <a class="ink-link" href={`${root}/methodology/`}>methodology</a> describes the models.
        The code and the forecast logs are open on
        <a class="ink-link" href={REPO}>GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="free-title">
      <h2 id="free-title">Keeping it free</h2>
      <p>
        Everything here is free to read, with no account and no paywall. The site is built once a day as static
        pages, so it costs little to run.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="indep-title">
      <h2 id="indep-title">Independence</h2>
      <p>
        This is an independent project, not affiliated with the EuroLeague or any club. Forecasts are for interest and
        are not betting advice.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .about h2 {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .about p {
    max-width: 62ch;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.55;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .about p + p {
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
</style>
